1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:02,730
You wake up nervous.

2
00:00:02,750 --> 00:00:04,255
Your heart's racing.

3
00:00:04,275 --> 00:00:05,970
Your hands are wet.

4
00:00:05,990 --> 00:00:07,805
Which is strange, because you've got

5
00:00:07,825 --> 00:00:09,875
nothing to be nervous about.

6
00:00:10,284 --> 00:00:12,614
Four hours away, your best friend has

7
00:00:12,634 --> 00:00:14,108
an exam at nine.

8
00:00:14,798 --> 00:00:16,703
From today, you feel everything she

9
00:00:16,723 --> 00:00:17,524
feels.

10
00:00:19,674 --> 00:00:20,524
Everything.

11
00:00:20,544 --> 00:00:23,004
The good, the bad, and the fourth coffee.

12
00:00:23,914 --> 00:00:25,519
Why are you breathing like that?

13
00:00:25,539 --> 00:00:26,353
Exam.

14
00:00:26,373 --> 00:00:27,764
You don't have an exam.

15
00:00:27,784 --> 00:00:28,740
I know!

16
00:00:29,790 --> 00:00:32,420
At nine, her exam starts, and your mind

17
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:34,035
goes completely blank.

18
00:00:34,055 --> 00:00:35,809
So the numbers for March are

19
00:00:35,829 --> 00:00:36,459
I'm sorry.

20
00:00:36,479 --> 00:00:37,446
Who are you?

21
00:00:38,496 --> 00:00:40,476
At ten, she has her fourth coffee.

22
00:00:40,496 --> 00:00:41,739
You have a meeting.

23
00:00:41,759 --> 00:00:43,274
Are you vibrating?

24
00:00:43,294 --> 00:00:45,018
Big fan of this quarter.

25
00:00:46,068 --> 00:00:47,973
At twelve, her exam is over and she's

26
00:00:47,993 --> 00:00:48,848
happy.

27
00:00:48,868 --> 00:00:50,073
So you're happy.

28
00:00:50,093 --> 00:00:52,489
You're so happy, you nearly hug Dana.

29
00:00:52,509 --> 00:00:53,977
Please don't.

30
00:00:54,127 --> 00:00:55,882
At one, she eats a pastry.

31
00:00:55,902 --> 00:00:57,372
You can't taste it.

32
00:00:57,392 --> 00:00:59,072
But you have never loved a sandwich

33
00:00:59,092 --> 00:00:59,958
this much.

34
00:01:00,948 --> 00:01:02,753
At three, she watches a horror film

35
00:01:02,773 --> 00:01:04,523
with her new flatmates.

36
00:01:04,813 --> 00:01:05,605
You don't.

37
00:01:06,514 --> 00:01:07,084
Sorry!

38
00:01:07,104 --> 00:01:07,904
Spreadsheet.

39
00:01:07,924 --> 00:01:09,340
Very scary numbers.

40
00:01:10,390 --> 00:01:12,595
At half five, her bus is late.

41
00:01:12,615 --> 00:01:14,095
You glare at a pigeon.

42
00:01:14,115 --> 00:01:15,855
The pigeon didn't do anything.

43
00:01:15,875 --> 00:01:16,763
Sorry.

44
00:01:16,913 --> 00:01:19,268
You just apologised to a pigeon.

45
00:01:19,288 --> 00:01:21,178
It's been a long day, and none of it

46
00:01:21,198 --> 00:01:22,206
was yours.

47
00:01:23,856 --> 00:01:26,061
By the evening, results are out tomorrow,

48
00:01:26,081 --> 00:01:27,516
and she's worried.

49
00:01:27,536 --> 00:01:28,716
So you're worried.

50
00:01:28,736 --> 00:01:30,187
And you can't turn it off.

51
00:01:30,207 --> 00:01:31,492
Why are you pacing?

52
00:01:31,512 --> 00:01:32,592
I'm not pacing.

53
00:01:32,612 --> 00:01:34,011
I'm walking with purpose.

54
00:01:34,031 --> 00:01:35,550
Can you feel me as well?

55
00:01:35,570 --> 00:01:36,231
No.

56
00:01:36,251 --> 00:01:37,001
Good.

57
00:01:37,801 --> 00:01:38,756
Did you sleep?

58
00:01:38,776 --> 00:01:39,876
Did you eat?

59
00:01:39,906 --> 00:01:41,516
Did you check question six?

60
00:01:41,536 --> 00:01:43,018
Why are you being my mum?

61
00:01:43,168 --> 00:01:44,823
Because her worry is sitting in your

62
00:01:44,843 --> 00:01:46,929
chest, and you want it out.

63
00:01:46,949 --> 00:01:48,404
You tell yourself you're helping.

64
00:01:48,424 --> 00:01:49,404
You're not.

65
00:01:49,424 --> 00:01:51,526
You just want the feeling to stop.

66
00:01:51,546 --> 00:01:52,571
Just relax.

67
00:01:52,611 --> 00:01:53,876
It'll be fine.

68
00:01:54,426 --> 00:01:55,806
Her worry goes up.

69
00:01:55,826 --> 00:01:57,911
You can feel exactly how much.

70
00:01:57,931 --> 00:01:58,311
Wow.

71
00:01:58,331 --> 00:01:58,931
Thanks.

72
00:01:58,951 --> 00:01:59,865
Going to bed.

73
00:02:00,915 --> 00:02:02,320
Now she's annoyed.

74
00:02:02,340 --> 00:02:04,415
And then, quietly, something else.

75
00:02:04,435 --> 00:02:05,465
Something heavy.

76
00:02:05,485 --> 00:02:07,640
Like a wet coat you can't take off.

77
00:02:09,590 --> 00:02:11,850
At midnight, you're lying in the dark,

78
00:02:11,870 --> 00:02:14,289
sad for a reason that isn't yours.

79
00:02:14,309 --> 00:02:15,388
So you call her.

80
00:02:15,408 --> 00:02:16,385
I'm fine.

81
00:02:17,035 --> 00:02:18,015
She's not.

82
00:02:18,035 --> 00:02:19,580
You can feel she's not.

83
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:20,850
You want to fix it.

84
00:02:20,875 --> 00:02:22,975
Tell her the exam went well.

85
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,830
Tell her the course is worth it.

86
00:02:24,850 --> 00:02:26,623
Tell her she'll make friends.

87
00:02:27,213 --> 00:02:29,648
But once, at a café, you learned not

88
00:02:29,668 --> 00:02:31,580
to answer things she hadn't said.

89
00:02:32,190 --> 00:02:33,917
You don't have to be fine.

90
00:02:34,717 --> 00:02:35,727
I just miss home.

91
00:02:35,747 --> 00:02:36,447
That's all.

92
00:02:36,487 --> 00:02:37,260
It's stupid.

93
00:02:37,280 --> 00:02:38,747
It's not stupid.

94
00:02:38,897 --> 00:02:40,852
And then you don't say anything else.

95
00:02:40,872 --> 00:02:42,668
You just stay on the line.

96
00:02:43,658 --> 00:02:44,683
Five minutes.

97
00:02:44,703 --> 00:02:45,408
Ten.

98
00:02:45,428 --> 00:02:46,823
Neither of you talks.

99
00:02:46,843 --> 00:02:48,723
And the heavy coat gets lighter.

100
00:02:48,743 --> 00:02:49,778
Not gone.

101
00:02:49,798 --> 00:02:50,618
Shared.

102
00:02:50,638 --> 00:02:53,107
You've felt her nervous, happy, terrified

103
00:02:53,127 --> 00:02:54,773
and annoyed today.

104
00:02:54,793 --> 00:02:56,447
This is the first feeling you didn't

105
00:02:56,467 --> 00:02:58,002
try to make go away.

106
00:02:58,712 --> 00:02:59,772
Are you still there?

107
00:02:59,792 --> 00:03:00,670
I'm here.

108
00:03:00,690 --> 00:03:01,695
You're smiling.

109
00:03:01,715 --> 00:03:02,760
I can hear it.

110
00:03:02,780 --> 00:03:04,617
Will you stay on until I fall asleep?

111
00:03:04,637 --> 00:03:05,397
Yeah.

112
00:03:06,147 --> 00:03:08,502
She falls asleep at twenty to one.

113
00:03:08,522 --> 00:03:10,902
You can feel it, like a lamp being turned

114
00:03:10,922 --> 00:03:12,880
down slowly in another city.

115
00:03:13,869 --> 00:03:16,439
The next morning, at nine, a feeling

116
00:03:16,459 --> 00:03:18,940
hits you so hard you drop your toast.

117
00:03:19,850 --> 00:03:20,793
She passed!

118
00:03:20,813 --> 00:03:22,012
Who passed what?

119
00:03:22,032 --> 00:03:22,974
Everything!

120
00:03:22,994 --> 00:03:24,535
Did you drop your toast?

121
00:03:24,555 --> 00:03:25,486
Worth it.

122
00:03:26,286 --> 00:03:26,976
Passed!

123
00:03:26,996 --> 00:03:27,901
Did you feel that?

124
00:03:27,921 --> 00:03:28,351
Felt it.

125
00:03:28,371 --> 00:03:29,688
Dropped my toast.

126
00:03:32,138 --> 00:03:34,018
Would you want to feel everything they

127
00:03:34,038 --> 00:03:34,672
feel?
